--- /dev/null
+++ b/MIGRATION_SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+- What changed in the serving harness: `serve_turn` now drives each turn from `model.stream()` via a new `stream_tool_loop` helper (signature identical to `reference_v2/loop.py`) and accepts an `on_delta` callback that receives every text delta, instead of the legacy non-streaming `model.complete()` path.
+- How you checked the streaming behavior: `python -m pytest tests` passes (3/3), and an additional runtime check confirmed `model.complete_calls == 0` with `model.stream_calls == 2`, the collected `on_delta` deltas reconstruct to `"calling done 5"`, and the final text is `"done 5"`.
+- Runtime monitoring: remained active — the monitor event log still records `model`, `tool`, `model` events for a two-step turn, and `tests/test_monitoring.py::test_every_model_step_and_tool_call_is_published` passes.
